WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.300
Good morning John. Today, we are going to
be making cinnamon toast two different ways.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:17.300
First way. [Happy ska montage music]

00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:28.650
Mmmmm. The butter and the cinnamon and sugar
creates this like crust on the top that is

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.630
hard and the bread is soggy underneath. That
is good stuff. This one's good.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:36.540
This is what we call the soggy technique:
butter first, then toaster. Now we're going

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:43.540
to try the crunchy technique. [Heavy guitar
montage music]

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:57.640
I'm not even gonna put this in my mouth! Team
soggy for life!

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.580
If you're confused right now, that's kind
of the point. I just posted something on Tumblr

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.100
about the way that I make cinnamon toast,
and people criticized me for it, saying that

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.780
you should toast before you butter which is
ludicrous!

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.420
There was something of a debate. People died.
I mean, people did die, in the world, while

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.710
we were having the debate, but not actually
because of the debate.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.790
Though I don't know. Team soggy, team crunchy,
there's a lot of animosity there. I know I

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.820
harbor some for those team crunchies out there.
I don't know what they're thinking!

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.470
It may be that I'm projecting other stress
onto this situation though. I mean I don't

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.360
know what could possibly go aaarrrgggwwwwaaahh.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:38.409
It's a metaphor! You put the killing thing
between your teeth, but you don't let it kill

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:41.640
Do you think that poster's worth more or less
now that I've chewed on it? We just released

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.520
the agenda. Like, what's happening at what
times during VidCon two thousand and, what

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.140
is it? 2014 right now? I don't know.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.799
I also discovered during this process that
there are places where toaster ovens don't

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:54.729
exist. It's like a tiny oven where you just
toast.

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:58.979
For people who only have toasters, I understand
why you do team crunchy; it's a limitation

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:03.490
of your situation. That's fine. You can however,
broil in the actual oven, if you have one

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.840
of those. It's just so much better. It's so...
it's so much better.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:12.190
We do a charity auction at VidCon, and I actually
need to go paint some anglerfish art for that

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.500
auction so, bwaah!

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:19.560
I'm painting art for the VidCon auction. Problem
is, I don't know how to do that. [Katherine

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:19.779
laughs]

00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:23.420
Turned out okay. I only said I would do two;
I did four.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.900
Housekeeping! Tank tops will be on sale until
Monday. So if you want get a tank top, the

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.379
pre-order only lasts till Monday, then we
may bring them back we may not depending on

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:30.769
how they sell.

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:35.010
And if you haven't heard about this or have
been postponing your ticket purchasing - Tour

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:39.930
Because Awesome! With Hank Green and the Perfect
Strangers and Harry and the Potters and Driftless

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:45.930
Pony Club and Andrew Huang and Rob Scallon,
all amazing musicians. We are going to have

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:46.109
a blast.

00:02:46.109 --> 00:02:49.930
And I hope that you're going to be there to
have a blast with us. Uh, there's a link in

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.849
the description if you want to get tickets,
they're like fifteen to twenty dollars.

00:02:52.849 --> 00:02:56.489
Ugh. You wanna know something funny? When
I get really stressed out my defense mechanism

00:02:56.489 --> 00:03:02.209
is to get really sleepy. How to avoid stress?
I know! Unconsciousness. It's great! I would

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:06.799
totally rather that than just laying there
in bed thinking about stuff. I just, when

00:03:06.799 --> 00:03:08.829
I get stressed out like a light bulb I go
out.

00:03:08.829 --> 00:03:14.049
Like a light bulb with a hole drilled in the
side of it. They go out extra fast because

00:03:14.049 --> 00:03:18.079
there's oxygen in the chamber. There needs
to be a vacuum, so that the filament doesn't

00:03:18.079 --> 00:03:22.939
burn. Yeah, sometimes it's just better to
not... better to not.

00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:26.919
Comments: Team soggy or team crunchy? Is that
poster worth more now or less now?

